tags: celaut-gateway

This layer is the gateway of a node: the celaut.Gateway service of celaut.proto,
carried by the layers grpc and bee-rpc.

The formal gives the RPCs of the gateway with their indices and their authentication
(rpc.* keys), the schema of each message (schema.* keys), the hash types, and the form
of each signed payload and of each digest. It is the formal that nodo sends today, with
the messages of the contract before the redesign. The redesign splits it into small
formals, one for each rule that two nodes must agree on (contract/PENDING.md).

The full prose of this layer comes from the comments of celaut.proto
(src/identity/protocol_doc.py). It is not copied here.

=== formal
amount=Amount.n: signed decimal integer string, in the MU of the receiving node
amount.negative=ModifyDepositInput.difference: a withdrawal from the instance
auth.client=Client at index 2 beside the payload at 1, any order; a local instance of the node needs none
auth.kinds=client,client-in-message,token,token+client,local-address,none
auth.token+client=instance token in the payload at 1; Client at index 2, needed only when the parent of the instance is a client, and then it must be that parent
chat.entry.client_ref=blake2b-256 hex of UTF-8 of celaut-chat-client:client_id
chat.entry.from_operator=1 when from_operator is true, else 0
chat.entry.genesis=blake2b-256 hex of UTF-8 of celaut-chat-genesis:client_ref#conversation_id, the prev_hash of the first entry of a conversation
chat.entry.hash=blake2b-256 hex of UTF-8 of celaut-chat-entry:client_ref|sequence|conversation_id|ts|from_operator|hex(body)|service|prev_hash
chat.entry.service='/'.join(hex(hash.type)~hex(hash.value) of each hash)~'/'.join(hex(tag) of each tag); empty when there is no service
chat.entry.signature=Peer.signature_scheme over UTF-8 of payload, lowercase hex
chat.entry.signature.payload=celaut-chat-signature:<public_key_hex>|<entry_hash>
client_binding.payload=celaut-client-binding:<public_key_hex>|<client_id>
client_binding.signature=Peer.signature_scheme, lowercase hex
client_id=32 lowercase hex characters
fault_evidence.digest=blake2b-256 hex of UTF-8 of reason|accused|statement digest of each statement|receipt digest of each receipt
fault_evidence.reasons=statement_inconsistent,killed_with_mu,statement_contradicts_receipt,maintenance_overcharged,instance_hibernated_unannounced,instance_stopped_unannounced
hash.type=the algorithm's digest of the empty input
introduce_peer.refused=REFUSED
keyvalue=producer: sorted by key (UTF-8 bytes), one entry per key, no empty key; reader: last entry wins
ledger_attestation.payload=celaut-ledger-attestation:<public_key_hex>
ledger_attestation.signature=the scheme of the proof's ledger; xattrs owner_public_key, owner_signature
offer.digest=blake2b-256 hex of UTF-8 of hex(cost.n)|hex(init_maintenance_cost.n)|hex(max_maintenance_cost.n)|maintenance_seconds_loop|launch_scarcity|price_bounded|price_volatility|volatility_period_seconds|valid_until|closes_at|on_close
offer.digest.hex=lowercase hex of UTF-8; numbers decimal; price_bounded 1 or 0; on_close the number of the enum
offer.digest.launch_scarcity='key=value' for each key, sorted by key, joined by ';'; empty when there is none
offer.digest.price_volatility=the 4 bytes of the float, big-endian, in lowercase hex
offer.signature=Peer.signature_scheme over UTF-8 of payload, lowercase hex
offer.signature.payload=celaut-price-offer:<public_key_hex>|<offer_digest>
peer.digest=blake2b-256 hex of UTF-8 of scheme|uris|contracts|rates|limits|resources|devices|activity_window
peer.digest.activity_window='-' when absent, else 'w:'+on_close number+':'+','.join(sorted(start_minute-end_minute))
peer.digest.contract_message=hex(ledger.formal)~','.join(sorted(ledger.tags))~ledger.prose~hex(protocol.formal)~','.join(sorted(protocol.tags))~protocol.prose~';'.join(key=hex(value) by key)
peer.digest.contracts='/'.join(sorted(contract_message~mu_per_unit.n))
peer.digest.devices='/'.join(sorted(protocol(architecture)~at_init~at_most~','.join(sorted(attach numbers))))
peer.digest.limits=';'.join(key=value by key)
peer.digest.protocol=hex(formal)~','.join(sorted(tags))~prose
peer.digest.rates=';'.join(key=amount.n by key)
peer.digest.resources='/'.join(sorted(protocol(architecture)~sysresources or '-'))
peer.digest.scheme=';'.join(sorted(protocol(component)))
peer.digest.sysresources=','.join(name=value or name= for blkio_weight,cpu_period,cpu_quota,mem_limit,disk_space)~';'.join(sorted(key=value or key=))
peer.digest.uri=ip~port~expiry~protocol(transport)~';'.join(sorted(protocol(stack)))
peer.digest.uris='/'.join(sorted(uri))
peer.signature=Peer.signature_scheme over UTF-8 of payload, lowercase hex
peer.signature.payload=<public_key_hex>|<ts>|<content_digest>
peer.ts=unix seconds; accepted only if greater than the last accepted ts for that public key
peer.uri.expiry=unix seconds; 0 means no estimate
pow.challenge=opaque; the caller sends it back unchanged
pow.retry=same client_id
pow.solution=blake2b-512 hex of UTF-8(challenge)||UTF-8(solution) ends with difficulty '0'
receipt.chain=blake2b-256 hex of UTF-8 of prev|seq|direction|length|blake2b-256 hex of payload; seq from 1; direction in or out; genesis 64 zeros; a tunnel records only the messages that its meter accepted
receipt.coverage=client-tunnel,instance-tap,counters-only
receipt.digest=blake2b-256 hex of UTF-8 of hex(kind)|peer_id|scheme|ts|execution_name|hex(service_id.type)~hex(service_id.value)|envs_digest|hex(initial_mu.n)|cpu_period|cpu_quota|mem_limit|disk_space|kernel|hex(devices)|hex(plane)|session|hex(slot)|seq|in_events|in_bytes|in_head|out_events|out_bytes|out_head|hex(mu_charged.n)|hex(coverage)|hex(capture_mode)|hex(degraded_reason)
receipt.digest.devices=the chips sorted, each in lowercase hex of UTF-8, joined by '/'; empty when there is none
receipt.digest.hex=lowercase hex of UTF-8; empty for an empty text; numbers decimal; an unused field empty or 0
receipt.digest.scheme=blake2b-256 hex of UTF-8 of peer.digest.scheme of signature_scheme
receipt.envs_digest=blake2b-256 hex of envs_salt || UTF-8 of '/'.join(origin~hex(name)~hex(value) sorted by UTF-8 of name); origin client or node; envs_salt exactly 16 bytes
receipt.execution_name=blake2b-256 hex of UTF-8(instance token) || the 32 raw bytes of the public key
receipt.execution_name.ref=in a DescendantTunnel stream: blake2b-256 hex of UTF-8(celaut-execution-ref:instance_ref) || the 32 raw bytes of the public key
receipt.kinds=start,checkpoint,close
receipt.ledger=detail.execution_name on start and tunnel movements; detail.session on tunnel movements of a receipt stream
receipt.signature=Peer.signature_scheme over UTF-8 of payload, lowercase hex
receipt.signature.payload=celaut-execution-receipt:<public_key_hex>|<receipt_digest>
receipt.tunnel=TokenMessage.receipts: ExecutionReceipt at index 2; a close when the stream stops normally
recursion_guard.token=opaque; the caller sends it again on a delegation
reputation_proof.amount=the score of the publisher for the object, as the absolute value; 0 for a fault report
reputation_proof.digest=blake2b-256 hex of UTF-8 of base|pow_nonce, where base is the blake2b-256 hex of UTF-8 of publisher|scheme|ts|'/'.join(opinion)|'/'.join(sorted(contract_message of each ledger_proofs))
reputation_proof.digest.opinion=hex(type)~hex(object)~amount~1 or 0~hex(content)~evidence digest or empty
reputation_proof.digest.scheme=peer.digest.scheme of signature_scheme
reputation_proof.fault_content=UTF-8 JSON with the keys reason, account_ref and seq
reputation_proof.signature=Peer.signature_scheme over UTF-8 of payload, lowercase hex
reputation_proof.signature.payload=celaut-reputation-proof:<public_key_hex>|<proof_digest>
reputation_proof.ts=unix seconds; accepted only if greater than the last accepted ts for that publisher
rpc.AssociateClient=in:1=celaut.Client;out:1=celaut.AssociateClientOutput;auth:client
rpc.Chat=in:1=celaut.ChatMessage;out:1=celaut.ChatAck;auth:client-in-message
rpc.GenerateClient=in:1=celaut.Client;out:1=celaut.Client,2=celaut.PoWRequired;auth:none
rpc.GenerateDepositToken=in:1=celaut.Client;out:1=celaut.TokenMessage;auth:client
rpc.GetBalanceStatement=in:1=celaut.BalanceStatementRequest,2=celaut.Client;out:1=celaut.BalanceStatement;auth:client
rpc.GetChatThread=in:1=celaut.ChatThreadRequest,2=celaut.Client;out:1=celaut.ChatThread;auth:client
rpc.GetClientMetrics=in:1=celaut.Client;out:1=celaut.Metrics;auth:client
rpc.GetMetrics=in:1=celaut.TokenMessage;out:1=celaut.Metrics;auth:token
rpc.GetPeerInfo=in:1=celaut.Client;out:1=celaut.Peer;auth:client
rpc.GetReputationProofs=in:1=celaut.Client;out:1=celaut.ReputationProof;auth:client
rpc.GetResourceAvailability=in:1=celaut.ResourceAvailabilityRequest,2=celaut.Client;out:1=celaut.ResourceAvailability;auth:client
rpc.GetService=in:1=celaut.Metadata.HashTag.Hash,2=celaut.Client;out:4=celaut.Metadata.HashTag.Hash,5=celaut.Metadata,6=celaut.Service;auth:client
rpc.GetServiceEstimatedCost=in:1=celaut.Client,2=celaut.RecursionGuard,3=celaut.Configuration,4=celaut.Metadata.HashTag.Hash,5=celaut.Metadata,6=celaut.Service,7=celaut.StartReference;out:1=celaut.EstimatedCost;auth:client
rpc.IntroducePeer=in:1=celaut.Peer,2=celaut.Client;out:1=celaut.RecursionGuard;auth:client
rpc.ListPeers=in:1=celaut.Client;out:1=celaut.Peer;auth:client
rpc.LocateShare=in:1=celaut.ShareLocationRequest,2=celaut.Client;out:1=celaut.ShareLocation;auth:client
rpc.ModifyDeposit=in:1=celaut.ModifyDepositInput,2=celaut.Client;out:1=celaut.ModifyDepositOutput;auth:token+client
rpc.ModifyServiceSystemResources=in:1=celaut.ModifyServiceSystemResourcesInput,2=celaut.Client;out:1=celaut.ModifyServiceSystemResourcesOutput;auth:token+client
rpc.Observe=in:1=celaut.ObserveRequest;out:1=celaut.ObserveEvent;auth:token
rpc.Payable=in:1=celaut.Payment,2=celaut.Client;out:1=buffer.Empty;auth:client
rpc.PushReputationProof=in:1=celaut.ReputationProof,2=celaut.Client;out:1=celaut.ReputationProofAck;auth:client
rpc.ResolveNetwork=in:1=celaut.Service.Network,2=celaut.Client;out:1=celaut.ConfigurationFile.NetworkResolution;auth:client
rpc.ServiceTunnel=in:0=bytes,1=celaut.TokenMessage,2=celaut.DescendantTunnel,3=celaut.Instance.Uri;out:0=bytes,2=celaut.ExecutionReceipt;auth:token
rpc.StartService=in:1=celaut.Client,2=celaut.RecursionGuard,3=celaut.Configuration,4=celaut.Metadata.HashTag.Hash,5=celaut.Metadata,6=celaut.Service,7=celaut.StartReference;out:1=celaut.ServiceInstance;auth:client
rpc.StopService=in:1=celaut.TokenMessage,2=celaut.Client;out:1=celaut.Refund;auth:token+client
